# tabulated-dataset v1
# key: attic_archons
# basis: attested
# source: "Archons of Athens", academickids.com encyclopedia (mirror of the
#   Wikipedia list of Athenian eponymous archons), saved to
#   ~/AgentWorkspaces/papers/calendars/attic_archons_reference.html.
# note: The eponymous archon of Athens gave his name to the civil year, which
#   ran from around midsummer (the month Hekatombaion, ~July) of the first BC
#   year to midsummer of the next -- so each archon-year straddles two of our
#   BC years (Solon 594/593).  Only securely-dated, unambiguously-named archons
#   are listed; homographic or doubly-attested names (e.g. Callias, held in
#   both 456/455 and 412/411) are omitted rather than guessed.  BC year is the
#   EARLIER (opening) year of the archon-year; astronomical opening year is
#   -(bc-1) and the span runs [1 Jul opening, 1 Jul next).
# columns: key  bc_year  english_name
solon        594  Solon
hipparchus   496  Hipparchus
themistocles 493  Themistocles
diognetus    492  Diognetus
phaenippus   490  Phaenippus
aristides    489  Aristides
calliades    480  Calliades
pythodorus   432  Pythodorus
nausinicus   378  Nausinicus
eucleides    403  Eucleides
